          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em combinatorial model category
            is a particularly tractable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure. (Notice however that there is also the, closely related, technical notion of a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tractable+model+category"} tractable model category
          %p
            Being combinatorial means that there is very strong control over the cofibrations in these model structures: there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            (meaning
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper class
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} generating (acyclic) cofibrations
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
          %p So as a slogan we have that
          .standout
            %p
              A combinatorial model structure is one that is generated from
              = succeed ":" do
                %em small data
          %p
            In fact, the combinatoriality condition is a bit stronger than that, as it requires even that
            %em every
            object is small and is the colimit over a small set of generating objects.
          %p
            There exist large classes of model categories that either are combinatorial or, if not, are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to ones that are. See the list of examples below.
          %p The relevance of combinatorial model categories is given more abstractly by the result that
          .standout
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} Combinatorial simplicial model categories
              are precisely those model categories that model
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentable (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories+-+introduction"} locally presentable categories - introduction
          %p
            There is also a more general class of model structures on locally presentable categories, namely
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+model+categories"} accessible model categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structures"} transferred model structures
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+model+category"} algebraic model category
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The following definition originates with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              %strong combinatorial
              if it is
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %p and
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated
                as a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Recall from the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              that this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              (i.e. a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              of generating
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              and a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              of generating trivial cofibrations in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cof
                    %mo =
                    %mi llp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi rlp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    cof = llp(rlp(I))
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi fib
                    %mo =
                    %mi rlp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    fib = rlp(J)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi fib
                    %mo ,
                    %mi cof
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} fib, cof \subset Mor(C)
              is the collection of fibrations and cofibration, respectively, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi llp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi rlp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} llp(S), rlp(S)
              is the collection of morphisms satisfying the left or right, respectively,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
              with respect to a collection of morphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Jeff Smith’s theorem,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SmithTheorem"} below
          %h2#characterization_theorems Characterization theorems
          %p There are two powerful theorems that characterize combinatorial model categories in terms of data that is often easier to handle:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"}> Jeff Smith
                ‘s theorem characterizes combinatorial model categories just in terms of weak equivalences and generating cofibrations, hence using only two third of the input data explicitly required. This greatly facilitates identifying combinatorial model category structures. For instance it helps to show that the left
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
                of certain combinatorial model categories is again a combinatorial model category.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dugger%27s+theorem"} Dugger's theorem
                shows that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model categories
                are, up to
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
                %em presentation
                in that they are
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global model structures on simplicial presheaves
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
                to show that simplicial combinatorial model categories are precisely the models for
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-categories
          %h3#SmithTheorem Smith’s theorem
          %p
            A central theorem about combinatorial model categories is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"}> Jeff Smith
              ‘s theorem
            which establishes the existence of combinatorial model category structures from a small amount of input data.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Jeff Smith’s theorem)
            %p For
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Arr
                          %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi Arr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr_W(C) \subset Arr(C)
                  an accessibly embedded
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Arr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(C)
                  on a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi Mor
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subset Mor(C)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subset Mor(C)
                  a small
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  (not a proper class) of morphisms of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  satisfies
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} 2-out-of-3
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi inj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inj(I) \subset W
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi cof
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof(I) \cap W
                  is closed under
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
            %p
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a combinatorial model category with
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  weak equivalences
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %li
                %p
                  cofibrations
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi cof
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi I
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof(I)
            %p Moreover, every combinatorial model category arises in this way.
          %p
            Here the notation is as described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi inj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi rlp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inj(I) = rlp(I)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi llp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi rlp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof(I) = llp(rlp(I))
          %p
            This statement was announced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
            in 1998 at a conference in Barcelona and appararently first appeared in print as (
            %a{:href => "#Beke"}> Beke, theorem 1.7
            ). The above formulation follows (
            %a{:href => "#Barwick"}> Barwick, prop 1.7
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              To prove the first part of the statement, that the given data encodes a combinatorial model category, it is sufficient to find a small set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi W
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    cof(J) = W \cap cof(I)
                    \\,.
            %p
              With that the statement follows using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              to show the existence of the required factorizations.
            %p
              To find this small set, we make use of the assumption that the subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Arr
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Arr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr_W(C) \subset Arr(C)
              of weak equivalences and commuting squares in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              between them is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible
              subcategory of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Arr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_0 \subset W
              such that every element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+colimit"} directed colimit
              over element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_0
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Arr
                        %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr_W(C)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal+number"} cardinal number
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_0
              are
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact
            %p
              Using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              factor every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Q
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_0
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi cell
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi I
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi inj
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi I
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \stackrel{\in cell(I)}{\to} R \stackrel{\in inj(I)}{\to}Q
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} 2-out-of-3
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inj(I) \subseteq W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to R
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              be the set of acyclic cofibratons
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to R
              so obtained.
            %p
              By the choice of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_0
              every morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi I
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    K &amp;\to&amp; M
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in I}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in W}}
                    \\\
                    L &amp;\to&amp; N
                    }
            %p
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Arr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(C)
              lifts through one of the components in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_0
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              (this mechanism is described in detail at
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi I
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %msub
                                    %mi W
                                    %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi N
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    K &amp;\to&amp; P &amp;\to&amp; M
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in I}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in W_0}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in W}}
                    \\\
                    L &amp;\to&amp; Q &amp;\to&amp; N
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              We can refine this to a factoring through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              as follows: by construction the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to Q
              factors as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi J
                      %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi inj
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi I
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \stackrel{\in J}{\to} R \stackrel{\in inj(I)}{\to}Q
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \to Q
              lifts to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \to R
              and we obtain the factorization
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi I
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi J
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    K &amp;\to&amp; P &amp;\to&amp; M
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in I}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in J}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in W}}
                    \\\
                    L &amp;\to&amp; R &amp;\to&amp; N
                    }
            %p
              of the original square from an element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              to an element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              through an element in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0102087"} Beke
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
              = succeed ":" do
                %strong solution set condition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              is “a solution set for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              at
              = succeed "\u201D)." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi W
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inj(J) \cap W \subseteq inj(I)
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi W
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{\in W}{\to} B
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              may be factored as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi cell
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi inj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \stackrel{\in cell(J)}{\to} C \stackrel{\in inj(J)}{\to} B
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} 2-out-of-3
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to B
              is in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi W
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inj(J) \cap W \subseteq inj(I)
            %p
              This we use to show that every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in cof(I) \cap W
              is in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cof
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof(J)
            %p
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in W
              we may factor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              as above and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in cof(I)
              we obtain a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi cell
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi J
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mi σ
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi inj
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi I
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\stackrel{\in cell(J)}{\to}&amp; C
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{f} &amp;{}^\sigma \nearrow&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in inj(I)}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{=}{\to}&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Rearranging this it becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              diagram in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Arr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(C)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi cell
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi J
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi σ
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi inj
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi I
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\stackrel{=}{\to}&amp; A &amp;\stackrel{=}{\to}&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^f &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in cell(J)}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^f
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\stackrel{\sigma}{\to}&amp;
                    C
                    \&amp;
                    \\stackrel{\in inj(I)}{\to}
                    \&amp;
                    B
                    }
            %p
              which shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a retract of an element in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cell
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi cof
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cell(J) \subset cof(J)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cof
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof(J)
            %p
              And the converse statement is immediate: by definition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset cof(I) \cap W
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof(J)
              is the saturation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              under the operation of forming retracts of transfinite compositions of pushouts of elements of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof(I) \cap W
              is assumed to be closed.
            %p
              In total we have indeed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof(J) = cof(I) \cap W
              which shows that the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              given determine a combinatorial model category.
            %p
              To see the converse, that every combinatorial model structure arises this way, it is sufficient to show that for every combinatorial model category the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Arr
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Arr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr_W(C) \subset Arr(C)
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
          %p For applications of this theorem, the following auxiliary statements are useful.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a combinatorial model category, the full subcategory inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi W
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Mor(C)_W \hookrightarrow Mor(C)
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
              on the weak equivalences is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible inclusion
              of an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
          %p
            This is due to Smith. A proof appears as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Dugger01"} Dugger 01, 7.4
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Barwick"} Barwick, prop. 1.10
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F : Mor(A) \to Mor(B)
            %p
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible functor
              between
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+categories"} arrow categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              be equipped with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Mor(W) \hookrightarrow Mor(B)
            %p
              on the weak equivalences is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible embedding
              of an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(A)
              on the pre-images
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{-1}(W)
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Beke"}> Beke, prop. 1.18
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By general properties of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+categories"} accessible categories
              (see there) the full inverse image along an accessible functor of a full accessible subcategory is again accessible.
          %h3#the_compactly_generated_left_proper_case_of_smiths_theorem The compactly generated left proper case of Smith’s theorem
          %p
            In the special case when weak equivalences are closed under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
            and the model structure is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper"} left proper
          %p
            The following formulation can be found as Proposition A.2.6.15 in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              of weak equivalences that turn it into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+category"} relative category
              and a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              of generating cofibrations. If the following conditions are satisfied, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper"} left proper
              model structure with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              as the set of generating cofibrations:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi inj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inj(I) \subset W
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  every element of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-cofibration"} h-cofibration
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %em perfect
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3+property"} 2-out-of-3 property
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
                  (in the category of morphisms in
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
                  by a set of morphisms.
            %p
          %h3#DuggerTheorem Dugger’s theorem
          %p
            The following theorem is precisely the model-category theory version of the statement that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
            arises as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization
            of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dugger%27s+theorem"}> Dugger's theorem
                )
            %p
              Every combinatorial model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
              to a left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S SPSh(K)_{proj}
              of the global projective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPSh(K)_{proj}
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi SPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Quillen
                    %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L_S SPSh(K)_{proj} \stackrel{\simeq_{Quillen}}{\to}
                    C
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Dugger01"}> Dugger 01, theorem 1.1
            ) building on results in (
            %a{:href => "#DuggerUniversalHomotopy"}> DuggerUniversalHomotopy
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p The proof proceeds (the way Dugger presents it, at least) in roughly three steps:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Use that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi sSet
                          %mi Quillen
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, sSet_{Quillen}]_{proj}
                  is in some precise sense the
                  %em homotopy-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi γ
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma : C \to B
                  from a plain category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  to a model category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  factors in an essentially unique way through the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi sSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : C \to [C^{op},sSet]
                  by a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                        %mover
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi R
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mover
                              %mi γ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi sSet
                          %mi Quillen
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi proj
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (\hat \gamma \dashv R) :
                        B
                        \\stackrel{\overset{\hat \gamma}{\leftarrow}}
                        {\underset{R}{\to}}
                        [C^{op}, sSet_{Quillen}]_{proj}
                        \\,.
                %p
                  The detailed definitions and detailed proof of this are discussed at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
              %li
                %p
                  For a given combinatorial model category
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %msubsup
                          %mi B
                          %mi λ
                          %mi cof
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C := B_\lambda^{cof}
                  the full
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
                  on a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
                  (guaranteed to exist since
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  is
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi λ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                  = succeed "s," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi λ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mover
                          %munder
                            %mo ↪
                            %mi R
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mover
                              %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi B
                          %mi λ
                          %mi cof
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi sSet
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        B \stackrel{\overset{\hat i}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\hookrightarrow}}
                        [(B_\lambda^{cof})^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
                %p
                  induced by the above statement from the inclusion
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %msubsup
                          %mi B
                          %mi λ
                          %mi cof
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : B_\lambda^{cof} \hookrightarrow B
                  exhibits
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  as a homotopy-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
                  in that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived
                  counit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi Q
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi R
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ≃
                        %mi Id
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat i \circ Q \circ R \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Id
                  (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
                  some cofibrant replacement functor) is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
                  weak equivalence on fibrant objects (recall from
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
                  the characterization of adjoints to full and faithful functors).
              %li
                %p
                  Define
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  to be the set of morphisms in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mi λ
                          %mi cof
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi sSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(C_\lambda^{cof})^{op}, sSet]
                  that the left
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat i \circ Q
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat i
                  (here
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
                  is some cofibrant replacement functor) sends to weak equivalences in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mi λ
                          %mi cof
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi sSet
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi proj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S [(C_\lambda^{cof})^{op},sSet]_{proj}
                  with respect to this set of morphisms and prove that this is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
                  to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %p Carrying this program through requires the following intermediate results.
            %p
              First recall from the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
              that to produce the Quilen adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\hat i \dashv R)
              from
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
              functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I : C \to [\Delta,B]
            %p
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi B
                        %mi λ
                        %mi cof
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : C= B_\lambda^{cof} \to B
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of this is a functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde I : C \times \Delta \to B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C \times \Delta \downarrow b)
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              induced by this functor.
            %p
              %strong Lemma
              (Dugger, prop. 4.2)
            %p
              For every fibrant object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
              we have that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hocolim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hocolim (C \times \Delta \downarrow b) \to B)
              is weakly equivalent to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi Q
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat i \circ Q\circ R (b)
            %p
              %strong Corollary
              (Dugger, cor. 4.4) The induced Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                    [C^{op}, sSet]
            %p is a homotopy-reflective embedding precisely if the canonical morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hocolim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    hocolim (C \times \Delta \downarrow b) \to b
            %p
              are weak equivalences for every fibrant object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
            %p …
          %p
            Notice that the theorem just mentions plain combinatorial model categories, not
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Funct
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Funct(C^{op}, SSet)
            is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            and its projective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+functors"} global model structure on functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi proj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(C^{op}, SSet)_{proj}
            is compatibly a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localizations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            for more details.) Therefore an immediate but very useful corollary of the above statement is
          %p
          #EveryCombinatorialModelCatQEquivalentToLeftProper.num_cor
            %h6 Corollary
            %p
            %p
              Every combinatorial model category is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
              to one which is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              %li
                %p
                  a left
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper model category
            %p
          %h3#tractable_combinatorial_model_categories Tractable combinatorial model categories
          %p
            A combinatorial model category is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tractable+model+category"} tractable model category
            precisely if the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            of generating cofibrations can be chosen such that all elements have a cofibrant object as domain.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
            combinatorial model category precisely if the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            of generating trivial cofibrations can be chosen with cofibrant domain.
          %p
            This are corollaries 2.7 and 2..8 in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~clarkbar/complete.pdf"} Bar
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#hocolims Homotopy colimits
          #CharacterizationOfFilteredHomotopyColimits.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              In a combinatorial model category, for every sufficiently large regular
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal+number"} cardinal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              the following holds:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
                  preserve weak equivalences;
              %li
                %p
                  hence
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
                  are already
                  = succeed "s." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+homotopy+colimit"} filtered homotopy colimit
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              This appears as proposition 7.3 in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0007068"} Dug00
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~clarkbar/complete.pdf"} Bar
            %p
              The point is to choose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              such that all domains and codomains of the generating cofibrations are
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              all its objects are
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
              for some cardinal
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              to be the maximum of these.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F, G : J \to C
              be
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to G
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              that is degreewise a weak equivalence. Using the functorial factorization provided by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              this may be factored as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to H \to G
              where the first transformation is objectwise an acyclic cofibration and the second objectwise an acyclic fibration, and by functoriality of the factorization this sits over a factorization
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi H
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lim_\to F \stackrel{\simeq}{\hookrightarrow} \lim_\to H \stackrel{}{\to}\lim_\to G
                    \\,.
            %p
              It remains to show that the second morphism is a weak equivalence. But by our factorization and by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} 2-out-of-3
              applied to our componentwise weak equivalences, we have that all its components
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(j) \to G(j)
              are acyclic fibrations.
            %p
              At
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
              it is described in detail how
              = succeed "-smallness" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              implies that morphisms from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              into a
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi j
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi j
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∃
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∀
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\cdots&amp;\to&amp;H(j-1) &amp;\to&amp; H(j) &amp;\to&amp; H(j+1) &amp;\to&amp; \cdots
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp;{}^{\mathllap{\exists \hat f}}\nearrow&amp;\downarrow &amp; \swarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;X&amp; \stackrel{\forall f}{\to} &amp;\lim_\to H
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p So given a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi H
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi I
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \lim_\to H
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in I}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\to&amp; \lim_\to G
                    }
            %p
              we are guaranteed, by the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} smallness
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              that we established above, a lift
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi H
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi I
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi rlp
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi I
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; H(j) &amp;\to&amp; \lim_\to H
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in I}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\in \mathrlap{\in rlp(I)}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\to&amp; G(j) &amp;\to&amp; \lim_\to G
                    }
            %p
              into some component at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \in J
              and hence a lift
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi H
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi rlp
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi I
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo →
                            %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; H(j) &amp;\to&amp; \lim_\to H
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in I}} &amp;
                    \\nearrow
                    \&amp; \downarrow^{\in \mathrlap{\in rlp(I)}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\to&amp; G(j) &amp;\to&amp; \lim_\to G
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Thereby
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\to H \to \lim_\to G
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi rlp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} rlp(I) \subset W
          %h3#bousfield_localization Bousfield localization
          %p
            Combinatorial model categories, like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+model+category"} cellular model categories
            have a good theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localizations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
            for more on this.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#basic_examples Basic examples
          %p Basic examples are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                with its standard
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                with the Joyal-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"}> model structure for quasi-categories
                ;
              %p
                notice that this is not directly a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              %ul
                %li
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+Cartesian+fibrations"} model structure for Cartesian fibrations
                  over the point.
            %li
              %p
                the category of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            %li
              %p
                the categories of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,r)
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+space"} Theta space
          %h3#cisinski_model_structures Cisinski model structures
          %p
            More generally, every
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure"} Cisinski model structure
            is combinatorial.
          %h3#derived_examples Derived examples
          %p Further classes of examples are obtained from such basic examples by localizing presheaf categories with values in these:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                a combinatorial model category and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
                the injective and projective
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Funct
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Funct(C,V)_{inj}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Funct
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Funct(C,V)_{proj}
                are again combinatorial model categories. See there for details.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                is a left or right
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper model category
                then so is
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Funct
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Funct(C,V)_{inj}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Funct
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Funct(C,V)_{proj}
                and hence the standard results of the theory of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
                applies, which ensures that all left Bousfield localizations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mi Funct
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S Funct(C,V)
                are again combinatorial model categories. Such local
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+homotopical+presheaves"} local model structures on homotopical presheaves
                includes notably the local
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %h3#from_cofibrantly_generated_model_categories From cofibrantly generated model categories
          %p
            Not every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
            is also a combinatorial model category.
          %p For instance:
          .num_example
            %h6#counterexample (Counter)example
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              with the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} model structure on topological spaces
              is cofibrantly generated, but not combinatorial. But it is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
              to a combinatorial model structure, namely to the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
          %p
            One might therefore ask which cofibrantly generated model categories are Quillen equivalent to combinatorial ones. It turns out that if one assumes the large-cardinal hypothesis
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vopenka%27s+principle"} Vopěnka's principle
            %em every
            cofibrantly generated model category is Quillen equivalent to a combinatorial one. In fact, if we slightly generalize the notion of “cofibrantly generated,” this statement is equivalent to Vopěnka’s principle. For a discussion of this see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"}> Jiří Rosický
              ,
              %em Are all cofibrantly generated model categories combinatorial?
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.muni.cz/~rosicky/papers/cof1.ps"}> ps
              )
          %p
            Although Vopěnka’s principle cannot be proven from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+cardinal"} large cardinal
            hypotheses go, this means that looking for cofibrantly generated model categories that are not Quillen equivalent to combinatorial ones is probably a waste of time. Certainly, all known cofibrantly generated model categories
            %em are
            Quillen equivalent to simplicial ones, usually in a fairly natural way.
          %h3#simplicial_combinatorial_model_categories Simplicial combinatorial model categories
          %p
            Those combinatorial model categories that are at the same time
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+categories"} simplicial model categories
            are precisely those that present
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} presentable (∞,1)-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
