          %h2#references References
          %p
            Much of the theory of combinatorial model categories goes back to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
          %p
            After
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
            presented his recognition theorem at a conference in Barcelona, its first appearance in a publication is apparently
          %ul
            %li#Beke
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tibor+Beke"}> Tibor Beke
              , Theorem 1.7 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sheafifiable homotopy model categories
              %strong 129
              3 (2000) 447-475 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0102087"}> arXiv:math/0102087
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100004722"} doi:10.1017/S0305004100004722
          %p An early explicit account of the notion of combinatorial model categories is in Section II of:
          %ul
            %li#Dugger01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Combinatorial+model+categories+have+presentations"} Combinatorial model categories have presentations
              %strong 164
              1 (2001) 177-201 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0007068"}> arXiv:math/0007068
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/aima.2001.2015"} doi:10.1006/aima.2001.2015
          %p
            (which goes on to state and proof
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dugger%27s+theorem"} Dugger's theorem
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Universal+homotopy+theories"} Universal homotopy theories
          %p The definition of combinatorial model categories is recalled also as:
          %ul
            %li#Barwick10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
                , Def. 1.3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On left and right model categories and left and right Bousfield localizations
                %strong 12
                2 (2010) 245–320
              %p
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4310/hha.2010.v12.n2.a9"}> doi:10.4310/hha.2010.v12.n2.a9
                , subsuming:
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2067"}> arXiv:0708.2067
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2832"} arXiv:0708.2832
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.3435"} arXiv:0708.3435
            %li#Lurie
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                , Def. A.2.6.1 in:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
                (2009)
          %p
            Smith’s theorem appears as
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie, A.2.6.10
            and as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Barwick"} Barwick, prop. 1.7
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
          %p Futher details are discussed in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"}> Jiří Rosický
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On combinatorial model categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2185"} arXiv:0708.2185
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Raptis"}> George Raptis
              ,
              %em Notes on combinatorial model categories
              2014/2020 (
              %a{:href => "https://graptismath.net/files/notes-comb-model-cat.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/RaptisCombinatorialModelCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+2-category"} localization of a 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
            of combinatorial model categories at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            and its equivalence to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+2-category"} homotopy 2-category
            of (locally) presentable
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivators"} derivators
          %ul
            %li#Renaudin06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olivier+Renaudin"}> Olivier Renaudin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Plongement de certaines théories homotopiques de Quillen dans les dérivateurs
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0603339"}> arXiv:math/0603339
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2009.02.014"} doi:10.1016/j.jpaa.2009.02.014
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#Low14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhen+Lin+Low"}> Zhen Lin Low
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The heart of a combinatorial model category
              = succeed ")" do
